<title>DENMARK: Danish Feb CPI flat, yr/yr at 2.0 pct (EU method).</title>
<headline>Danish Feb CPI flat, yr/yr at 2.0 pct (EU method).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish consumer prices were unchanged in February 1997 from January and 2.0 percent higher than in February 1996, the National Statistics Office said on Friday.  </p>
<p>    NEW EU FORMULA	     Feb 1997   Jan 1997  Feb 1996</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)	0.0	   +0.3	+0.6</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	 +2.0	  +2.6	+1.2</p>
<p>    Index (base 1994)	    101.0	 101.0     99.0</p>
<p>NATIONAL FORMULA</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)	0.0	   +0.2	+0.6</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	 +2.2	  +2.7	+1.8</p>
<p>    Index (base 1980)	    202.0	 202.0     197.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Average analyst expectations were for a 2.4 percent yr/yr rise from February 1996 according to the national formula.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
